      "issue": "Crafting sandstone_stairs requires knowing the stair recipe pattern (6 blocks in a 3x3 grid: bottom-left, middle-left + middle-center, top-left + top-center + top-right). This is a standard Minecraft recipe but not obvious to a non-expert agent. However, since the task is explicitly 'craft to sandstone_stairs' and a crafting table is provided, most agents with basic Minecraft training should handle this.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "target_agent": "TaskSelectorAgent"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The player must recognize the visual difference between smooth_sandstone (flat, uniform texture) and regular sandstone (banded horizontal pattern) to know which blocks to mine. The textures are distinct but a non-expert might not immediately identify smooth_sandstone by sight alone. However, since the entire west face is smooth_sandstone and it's the only entry point, the player will naturally mine it regardless of identification.",
      "severity": "low",
      "target_agent": "SceneDesignerAgent"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The player needs to know that smooth_sandstone requires a pickaxe to mine (hand mining is extremely slow and drops nothing). A stone pickaxe IS provided, so this is handled — but the player must know to equip and use it. This is basic Minecraft knowledge.",
